course: dictionary
lesson: 6260
title: Molluscs: soft bodies, no backbone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mollusc is an animal with a soft body and no backbone. Many molluscs have a hard shell to protect them, but not all of them do.
explain: Snails, slugs, clams, mussels and oysters are molluscs. So are octopuses and squid, even though they have no outer shell.
explain: Context helps here. «Octopuses, squid and cuttlefish are molluscs, cousins of snails, whose shells have shrunk inside or vanished» tells you that octopuses are related to snails, even though they look very different. A shell is not what makes an animal a mollusc. Its soft body and lack of a backbone are.
fact: A mollusc is an animal with a soft body and no backbone.
fact: Many molluscs have a hard shell, but not all of them do.
fact: Snails, slugs, clams, mussels, oysters, octopuses and squid are all molluscs.
fact: Scientists call molluscs invertebrates, a huge group that lives on land, in fresh water and in the sea.
fact: «Molluscs and crustaceans» are two different groups of animals, so do not mix them up.
exercise: Which of these animals is a mollusc? | Spider | *Mussel | Frog | Hedgehog
exercise: «Octopuses, squid and cuttlefish are molluscs, cousins of snails.» What do octopuses and squid have in common with snails? | They both live only on land | *They are both molluscs | They both fly | They both have backbones
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Octopuses, squid and cuttlefish are molluscs... shape-changing hunters» that means able to change its form. | clever | *shape-changing | soft | hunters
test: Does a mollusc have a backbone? | *No, molluscs have no backbone | Only sometimes, when it is old | Yes, always | Only the big ones
test: Which of these is NOT a mollusc? | Oyster | *Crab | Snail | Octopus
exam: Why are octopuses and squid still molluscs even though they have no outer shell? | Because they have a backbone | *Because they have a soft body and no backbone | Because they live in the sea | Because they are slugs
